{
  "title": "Mirth Connect \u2014 healthcare (1,170\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Mirth Connect\nDomain: healthcare | Scale: large | Stars: 1,170\nProblem: Healthcare organizations need to exchange data between systems using different message standards and protocols. Mirth Connect provides an integration engine that filters, transforms, routes, and extracts healthcare messages across disparate systems.\nTarget users: Healthcare IT integrators, Health Information Exchanges (HIEs), Hospitals and large healthcare entities, Small to medium medical practices, Healthcare software developers\nCore features: Message filtering and routing between healthcare systems; Message transformation between standards (e.g., HL7 to XML); Channel-based message pathway configuration via Administrator UI; Data extraction and push/pull to/from databases; Plugin and connector extension system; Command Line Interface for scripting and server management; Embedded web server and web application hosting; Multi-server connection management via Administrator Launcher\nIntegrations: HL7 (v2/v3), XML, Apache Derby (embedded database), External relational databases (configurable backend), Log4j\nTech stack: Java Swing (Administrator UI) with JavaScript/HTML/CSS for embedded web components + Java + Apache Derby (embedded default), configurable external RDBMS + Embedded Jetty web server, cross-platform installer (Windows/Linux/macOS)\nKey libraries: Log4j, Jetty, PLSQL (database scripts)\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Extension-first design: the plugin/connector system allows the core engine to remain stable while new protocols and transformations are added as extensions in the /extensions directory.\n- Embedded database strategy lowers barrier to entry by shipping with Apache Derby, while still supporting external enterprise databases for production deployments.\n- Separation of client and server libraries (client-lib vs server-lib) enables the Administrator UI to be launched remotely against multiple server instances, decoupling management tooling from the runtime engine.\n- Channel abstraction (filter \u2192 transform \u2192 route) provides a uniform pipeline model that isolates each integration concern, making complex multi-system workflows composable and auditable.",
